.TH SYS_VM_SLABS 2 "May 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_vm_slabs \- query slab allocator statistics
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_vm_slabs(sys_slabinfo_t *" slabs ", size_t *" count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_vm_slabs ()
enumerates UMA zones (Substrate's slab allocator).  Each entry is
a
.B sys_slabinfo_t :
.PP
.RS
.nf
typedef struct sys_slabinfo {
    char     name[32];
    uint32_t active;
    uint32_t total;
    uint32_t objsize;
    uint32_t slabs;
    uint32_t pages_per_slab;
} sys_slabinfo_t;
.fi
.RE
.PP
On entry
.I *count
is the array capacity; on return it is the actual number of UMA
zones.  Until UMA grows a public iterator the syscall returns
.IR *count " = 0"
and writes nothing — a graceful "no data" answer rather than
.BR ENOSYS .
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success; on failure -1 and
.I errno
is set per the error contract.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I slabs
or
.I count
is NULL.
.TP
.B EFAULT
either pointer is unmapped.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_vm_stats (2),
.BR sys_vm_buffers (2),
.BR sysinfo (2)
